# Project context

LitecoinDevKit fork of wizardsardine/liana. Entry point: `AGENTS.md`. Living roadmap: `docs/PLAN.md`.

## Status

- Phase 0 (scaffold + docs): done
- Phase 1 (transparent Litecoin port): not started — no LTC code yet; daemon/GUI are still Bitcoin upstream
- Not mainnet-ready; do not invent Litecoin or MWEB behavior in code or copy

## Architecture

Two ledgers under one UI. Transparent stays Liana-shaped; MWEB is additive in `lianad`. Details: `docs/PLAN.md`.

- Three stores, never merge: transparent UTXOs | MWEB coins | recovery package backup
- Vault: Script `older(N)`. Private: `lock_height` packages + heir backup (feature parity, not mechanism parity)
- Never index HogAddr as transparent UTXOs
- Depend on LitecoinDevKit; never embed Nexus / `lndltc` / in-process `mwebd`
- Thin port + external oracle (alias over rewrite; golden/reference tests): `doc/AI_NATIVE_FORKING.md`

## Crates

| Crate | Role |
|-------|------|
| `liana` | Policy, descriptors, spend/recovery, signer |
| `lianad` | Daemon: backends, DB, JSON-RPC over UDS |
| `liana-gui` / `liana-ui` | Iced UI / design system |
| `liana-connect` / `liana-business` | Out of v1 LTC scope |

## Fork hygiene

Remotes: `origin` = LitecoinDevKit/liana-ltc; `upstream` = wizardsardine/liana. Details: `UPSTREAM.md`.

On merge conflicts: keep this fork’s README / `docs/PLAN.md` / `UPSTREAM.md`; take upstream for untouched daemon/GUI until Phase 1+ ports diverge.

Prefer regular merges of `upstream/master`. `master` tracks upstream; LTC product work goes on `litecoin` once Phase 1 starts (solo may push focused commits; PRs for external/large/funds work — `CONTRIBUTING.md`). Read `docs/PLAN.md` before large changes; update it when phases complete. Current focus when coding: Phase 1 transparent port — not MWEB recovery.
